<!--
    kuna issue testcase: the Listing walk adds the case bodies of a provably
    bounded i386 absolute-table switch (`option x86listingswitch on|off`,
    default-OFF).

    Issue:      kuna GH-299 - aif plants mid-function entries; on i386 the
                discovery walk stops at every jmp [idx*4 + table], so a case
                body that opens with a prologue becomes a sub_ in the middle of
                its dispatcher.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - post-walk switch reconciliation
                (`listing/kuna_x86listingswitch.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option x86listingswitch on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `x86listingswitch_i386` (source `x86listingswitch_i386.s`
    beside it): a stripped i386 ELF whose `_start` calls 22 leaves that open
    with `push esi; push ebx`, then `dispatch` at 0x10016c (`cmp eax,4; ja
    default; jmp [eax*4 + 0x101000]`, five cases), `sdispatch` at 0x100206
    (the same shape behind a signed `jg`, three cases) and `lone_called` at
    0x100190.  Each case of `dispatch` opens with the leaves' prologue, calls
    its own callee and returns; the cases sit around `lone_called` and around
    `lone_free` at 0x1001b0 (preceded by 12 bytes of int3 fill), which nothing
    references.  The word after the five-entry table points to `independent`
    at 0x10023a, which only that word names.

    Pass 1 (`mode aggressive`, shipped default) reproduces the bug: the gap
    walk lists the five cases (0x10017c, 0x100186, 0x10019a, 0x1001ba,
    0x1001c4) as functions, and misses two of their callees (0x1001de,
    0x1001f2).
    Pass 2 (`mode aggressive`, `option x86listingswitch on`) proves the bound
    of five, decodes the cases as the dispatcher's code and lists none of them;
    the five callees are found through the calls in the cases.  In both passes
    the dispatcher decompiles to the same five-case switch, `lone_called`,
    `lone_free` and `independent` stay functions (the sixth table word is not
    read), and the signed dispatch's cases stay listed (a signed bound reads
    nothing).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
